The lock-free structures in libs/shm — the SPSC ring, the broadcast ring and
the seqlock table — are original implementations written for this project.
They apply long-published techniques (false-sharing padding, cached counterpart
indices, seqlock validated reads) that are not any one project's to license,
and their shapes follow from a requirement those techniques were not written
for: living inside a memory segment that two processes map at once.

Third-party code is used through the dependencies declared in conanfile.py,
each under its own licence.
